Push button projects Overview

This folder contains a collection of basic RGB LED projects created to explore and understand the fundamentals of programming RGB LEDs using an ESP32.
Each project focuses on a different lighting behavior or control technique, helping build a strong foundation before moving on to more advanced 
electronics and embedded systems projects.

These examples demonstrate concepts such as digital output, PWM brightness control, timing with delays, sequencing multiple RGB LEDs,creating lighting
animations, and generating random patterns. They also serve as reference implementations that can be reused in future robotics, IoT, and embedded 
system projects

